   "source": [
    "# Recurrent Neural Network\n",
    "\n",
    "A **Recurrent Neural Network (RNN)** is a type of neural network designed for **sequential data** where the order matters. Unlike standard feedforward neural networks, RNNs have a form of **memory** that allows them to use information from previous inputs while processing current inputs.\n",
    "\n",
    "RNNs are widely used in:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Natural language processing (text, translation, chatbots)\n",
    "* Speech recognition\n",
    "* Time-series forecasting\n",
    "* Video analysis\n",
    "* Music generation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why Regular Neural Networks Struggle with Sequences**\n",
    "\n",
    "A normal feedforward neural network assumes:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Inputs are independent\n",
    "* Input size is fixed\n",
    "* No temporal relationship exists\n",
    "\n",
    "But many real-world problems are sequential:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Task                | Sequence Example                     |\n",
    "| ------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n",
    "| Sentence prediction | \"I love deep ...\" → \"learning\"       |\n",
    "| Stock prediction    | Yesterday affects today              |\n",
    "| Speech recognition  | Previous sounds affect current sound |\n",
    "| Weather forecasting | Past temperatures matter             |\n",
    "\n",
    "To solve this, we need a model that remembers previous information. That is where RNNs come in.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Core Idea\n",
    "\n",
    "An RNN processes data **step by step** while maintaining a hidden memory state.\n",
    "\n",
    "At each time step:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. It receives current input\n",
    "2. Combines it with previous hidden state\n",
    "3. Produces:\n",
    "   * new hidden state\n",
    "   * output\n",
    "\n",
    "### RNN Structure\n",
    "\n",
    "At time step $t$:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Input: $x_t$\n",
    "* Hidden state: $h_t$\n",
    "* Output: $y_t$\n",
    "\n",
    "The hidden state carries information from previous steps.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "![CNN Architecture](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook-old/removed/images/rnn/rnn.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Mathematical Formulation\n",
    "\n",
    "The hidden state update is:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "h_t = \\tanh(W_{xh}x_t + W_{hh}h_{t-1} + b_h)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Output computation:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "y_t = W_{hy}h_t + b_y\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Symbol     | Meaning                  |\n",
    "| ---------- | ------------------------ |\n",
    "| $x_t$      | Input at time ($t$)        |\n",
    "| $h_t$      | Hidden state             |\n",
    "| $W_{xh}$   | Input-to-hidden weights  |\n",
    "| $W_{hh}$   | Hidden-to-hidden weights |\n",
    "| $W_{hy}$   | Hidden-to-output weights |\n",
    "| $b_h, b_y$ | Biases                   |\n",
    "| $\\tanh$    | Activation function      |\n",
    "\n",
    "Mathematical intuition is same as basic neural network, just the equation is different. But introduces a recurrent state that makes the model time-dependent and shares parameters across time steps, which changes how information and gradients flow.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Understanding the “Memory”\n",
    "\n",
    "The hidden state acts like memory.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example sentence:\n",
    "\n",
    "> “The movie was not good”\n",
    "\n",
    "When predicting sentiment at “good”, the word “not” from earlier is important.\n",
    "\n",
    "The RNN hidden state stores contextual information from previous words.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Unrolling an RNN\n",
    "\n",
    "An RNN can be visualized as being “unrolled” through time.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example for sequence:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_1, x_2, x_3\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "becomes:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "h_0 \\rightarrow h_1 \\rightarrow h_2 \\rightarrow h_3\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Each step shares the same weights.\n",
    "\n",
    "This weight sharing is important because:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Fewer parameters\n",
    "* Handles variable-length sequences\n",
    "* Learns temporal patterns\n",
    "\n",
    "## Types of RNN Architectures\n",
    "\n",
    "### One-to-One\n",
    "\n",
    "This is actually a standard neural network (not sequence modeling).\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: Image classification\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x \\rightarrow y\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This is NOT a sequence problem, so RNN is unnecessary in real life."
   ]
