   "source": [
    "**RepeatVector**\n",
    "\n",
    "Repeats a single vector multiple times (copies it across time steps).\n",
    "\n",
    "* In a **one-to-many RNN**, you start with: One input → One vector`\n",
    "* But RNN needs: `Sequence input (time steps)`\n",
    "* So we *duplicate* the vector across time.\n",
    "\n",
    "Shape transformation\n",
    "\n",
    "* If input is: `(batch, features)`\n",
    "* After RepeatVector: `(batch, timesteps, features)`\n",
    "\n",
    "If input:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "[0.5, 0.8]   → shape (features,)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Output:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "[\n",
    "  [0.5, 0.8],\n",
    "  [0.5, 0.8],\n",
    "  [0.5, 0.8],\n",
    "  [0.5, 0.8]\n",
    "]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "So it becomes a sequence of identical vectors.\n",
    "\n",
    "It is like saying:\n",
    "\n",
    "> “Take one idea and feed it step-by-step into a sequence model.”\n",
    "\n",
    "**TimeDistributed**\n",
    "\n",
    "Applies the same layer independently to every time step.\n",
    "\n",
    "RNN output is often:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "(batch, timesteps, features)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "But Dense layer normally expects:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "(batch, features)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "So we need a way to apply Dense to each timestep separately.\n",
    "\n",
    "Shape transformation\n",
    "\n",
    "* Input: `(batch, timesteps, features)`\n",
    "* Output: `(batch, timesteps, output)`\n",
    "\n",
    "If input:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "[\n",
    "  [h11, h12],\n",
    "  [h21, h22],\n",
    "  [h31, h32]\n",
    "]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Output:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "[\n",
    "  [y11, y12, ..., y1_10],\n",
    "  [y21, y22, ..., y2_10],\n",
    "  [y31, y32, ..., y3_10]\n",
    "]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Each timestep is processed independently.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "It is like:\n",
    "\n",
    "> “Apply the same classifier to every word in a sentence.”\n",
    "\n",
    "### Many-to-One\n",
    "\n",
    "Sequence input → single output.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: Sentiment analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_1,x_2,x_3 \\rightarrow y\n",
    "$$"
   ]
