    "## Charecterstics\n",
    "\n",
    "### Comparison:RNN vs LSTM\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature                | RNN        | LSTM              |\n",
    "| ---------------------- | ---------- | ----------------- |\n",
    "| Memory                 | Short-term | Long + short-term |\n",
    "| Handles long sequences | Poorly     | Very well         |\n",
    "| Vanishing gradient     | Severe     | Reduced           |\n",
    "| Complexity             | Simple     | More complex      |\n",
    "| Training speed         | Faster     | Slower            |\n",
    "| Accuracy               | Lower      | Higher            |\n",
    "\n",
    "# Gated Recurrent Unit\n",
    "\n",
    "It is a type of **Recurrent Neural Network (RNN)** introduced to solve the major problem of standard RNNs:\n",
    "\n",
    "* vanishing gradients\n",
    "* poor long-term memory\n",
    "\n",
    "GRU was proposed as a simpler alternative to LSTM.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Evolution: RNN → LSTM → GRU**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Memory Handling         |\n",
    "| ----- | ----------------------- |\n",
    "| RNN   | Simple hidden state     |\n",
    "| LSTM  | Cell state + gates      |\n",
    "| GRU   | Simplified gated memory |\n",
    "\n",
    "GRU keeps the advantages of LSTM while using:\n",
    "\n",
    "* fewer parameters\n",
    "* simpler architecture\n",
    "* faster training\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main Idea of GRU**\n",
    "\n",
    "GRU introduces **gates** to control information flow.\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike LSTM:\n",
    "\n",
    "* no separate cell state\n",
    "* hidden state itself acts as memory\n",
    "\n",
    "GRU uses only:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Update Gate\n",
    "2. Reset Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "This simplicity makes GRU computationally efficient.\n",
    "\n",
    "## GRU Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "At time step $t$:\n",
    "\n",
    "Inputs:\n",
    "\n",
    "* current input ($x_t$)\n",
    "* previous hidden state ($h_{t-1}$)\n",
    "\n",
    "Output:\n",
    "\n",
    "* new hidden state ($h_t$)\n",
    "\n",
    "![GRU Architecture](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook-old/removed/images/rnn/gru.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Core Components of GRU**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Gate            | Purpose                            |\n",
    "| --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n",
    "| Update Gate     | How much old memory to keep        |\n",
    "| Reset Gate      | How much old information to forget |\n",
    "| Candidate State | New information                    |\n",
    "| Hidden State    | Final memory/output                |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Update Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "Determines how much previous memory should be preserved.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "z_t = \\sigma(W_z x_t + U_z h_{t-1})\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "* $z_t$ = update gate\n",
    "* $\\sigma$ = sigmoid function\n",
    "\n",
    "Output range:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "0 \\rightarrow 1\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Interpretation:\n",
    "\n",
    "* close to 1 → keep old memory\n",
    "* close to 0 → replace with new memory\n",
    "\n",
    "### Reset Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "Controls how much previous information to forget.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "r_t = \\sigma(W_r x_t + U_r h_{t-1})\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Interpretation:\n",
    "\n",
    "* small value → ignore previous memory\n",
    "* large value → use previous memory heavily\n",
    "\n",
    "### Candidate Hidden State\n",
    "\n",
    "Creates new candidate memory.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\tilde{h} \\odot t = \\tanh(W_h x_t + U_h(r_t * h*{t-1}))\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Important idea:\n",
    "\n",
    "> Reset gate filters previous memory before combining it with current input.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Final Hidden State\n",
    "\n",
    "Combines:\n",
    "\n",
    "* old memory\n",
    "* candidate memory\n",
    "$$\n",
    "h_t = (1-z_t) * h_{t-1} + z_t * \\tilde{h}_t\n",
    "$$\n",
    "This is the core GRU update equation.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Example Walkthrough\n",
    "\n",
    "Sentence:\n",
    "```\n",
    "[\n",
    "[\"I\", \"love\", \"machine\", \"learning\"]\n",
    "]\n",
    "```\n",
    "1. Time Step 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Input:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_1 = I\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Initial hidden state:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "h_0 = 0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "GRU stores information about subject.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Time Step 2\n",
    "\n",
    "Input:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_2 = love\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Update gate decides:\n",
    "\n",
    "* keep subject info\n",
    "* add emotional context\n",
    "\n",
    "Hidden state now contains: `I love`\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Time Step 3\n",
    "\n",
    "Input:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_3 = machine\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Reset gate may reduce less useful information. Model updates semantic context.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Time Step 4\n",
    "\n",
    "Input:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_4 = learning\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Final hidden state captures meaning: `I love machine learning`\n",
    "\n",
    "## Intuition Behind GRU\n",
    "\n",
    "### Update Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "Acts like a smart balance:\n",
    "\n",
    "* keep important past information\n",
    "* update irrelevant information\n",
    "\n",
    "### Reset Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "Acts like selective forgetting.\n",
    "\n",
    "Useful when:\n",
    "\n",
    "* old context no longer matters\n",
    "* sequence topic changes\n",
    "\n",
    "### Visual Intuition\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose sentence:\n",
    "\n",
    "> “I grew up in Bangladesh ... now I live in Canada”\n",
    "\n",
    "When processing “Canada”:\n",
    "\n",
    "* reset gate may reduce importance of old location context\n",
    "* update gate stores new relevant context\n",
    "\n",
    "GRU dynamically updates memory.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Bidirectional GRU\n",
    "\n",
    "Normal GRU:\n",
    "\n",
    "* reads left → right\n",
    "\n",
    "Bidirectional GRU:\n",
    "\n",
    "* left → right\n",
    "* right → left\n",
    "\n",
    "Useful when future context matters.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: `He sat on the bank`\n",
    "\n",
    "Later words help determine meaning of “bank”."
   ]
